@page "/personal/index.html"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "static_void - yt6983138";
    ViewData["ActiveTab"] = "Index";

    Layout = "_Layout";
}

@section Headers {
    <style>
        body {
            padding: 40px 5px;
        }

        #main {
            width: 100%;
        }
    </style>
}

<win-dialog id="main" title="About me">
    <p>
        Hello! This is my personal website, this website is about to introduce me and share techniques that took
        me really long to find. <br />
        <button onclick="document.getElementById('blog-link').click()">Checkout my blog</button>
        <button onclick="document.getElementById('tools-link').click()">Checkout the web tools</button><br />
        You might have heard me on Discord or other platforms in various way. <br />
        I'll introduce me in few different sections.
    </p>
    <h1>1. As a Developer</h1>
    <p>
        You may known me from my most used project - <a href="https://github.com/yt6983138/PSLDiscordBot">PSLDiscordBot</a>, 
        a Phigros score lookup Discord bot. <br />
        It was made because I realized there was no Phigros score lookup bots in Discord, so I decided to make one, to make everyone 
        and my life easier. <br /><br />

        If you are also a developer, you may want to checkout <a href="https://github.com/yt6983138">my personal page</a>.<br />
        I also have made other projects:
        <ol>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/yt6983138/PhigrosLibraryCSharp">PhigrosLibraryCSharp</a>: A unofficial read-only Phigros save client, 
                also the underlying core library for PSLDiscordBot.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/yt6983138/PhigrosSaveDumper">PhigrosSaveDumper</a>: A Phigros save analyzer/debugger.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/yt6983138/PhiInfo">PhiInfo</a>: A Phigros asset extractor fork aimed to improve developer experience and performance.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/yt6983138/OsuLazerFSMounter">OsuLazerFSMounter</a>: A virtual filesystem plugin for osu!lazer.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/yt6983138/GraphwarSFX">GraphwarSFX</a>: An AOT .NET JVM agent to add sound effects to Graphwar.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/yt6983138/10CSS">10CSS</a>: A Windows 10 stylesheet library. 
                This page is made using this library.</li>
        </ol><br /><br />

        I started my programming journey 2 years ago (actually 8 years ago if things useless counted), and begin with
        C#. <br />
        I absolutely love it because its extensibility and syntax richness, you can do so many things with it,
        from low level system interoperation to high level web application. <br />
        I started using it because I wanted to create a screen widget for my class, our teacher didn't put a clock in
        classroom, so I decided to make a draggable clock on screen, and it turned out quite well. <br />

        Then I'm into web development, using Blazor WASM (though turned out to be a terrible idea for simple websites),
        remember I created PSLDiscordBot? There was, in fact, an earlier version of it done using web technique,
        it was called <a href="https://github.com/yt6983138/yt6983138.github.io">RksReaderEnhanced</a> (though it wasn't
        maintained anymore.) <br /><br />

        You may ask why didn't I continue using the web to do score lookups? Well, I realized my frontend skill is shit, 
        so I decided to redo it using Discord with since it provides me an existing framework and UI to do things,
        also it has much larger userbase.<br /><br />

        Now, I'm into many frameworks, ASP.NET MVC, EF Core, Blazor SSR, Blazor WASM, and even created one on
        my own (<a href="https://github.com/yt6983138/PSLDiscordBot">PSLDiscordBot.Framework</a>).
    </p>

    <h1>2. As a Rhythm Game Player (<a href="https://osu.ppy.sh/users/20208991">osu! Profile</a>)</h1>
    <p>
        I started playing Phigros at 2022, which well, I don't play it anymore. <br />
        (I know I still maintain tools about it but I don't really play, I guess that's what rhythm game becomes lol) <br />
        It's really fun, but the lack of phone performance and a tablet make pushing scores extremely hard so I stopped playing it,
        now my RKS is just stuck at 15.634. <br /><br />

        Then I went into osu!mania, I liked the simpleness (ps. they are not) it offer, you just need to have a keyboard to play it,
        no need for phone and tablet. And there are much more songs to play, so I just stayed there until now. <br />
        <sub>Tbh I felt like I live 10 years ago lmao, not familiar with phones but only with a PC</sub><br /><br />

        I decided to stay with 6k, since 4k is a bit too boring, no fancy patterns. And 7k is a pain to play because I suck at 
        controlling my thumb.<br />
        Now I've passed 6k LN 9 dan and Regular 7 dan (I even got Terra dan stream by 95.4%), really felt fun with it.
    </p>
</win-dialog>